3:  * update_memory.js - Syncs the <aidd_project_memory> block in AI context files.
4:  *
5:  * Scans aidd_docs/memory/ and updates the <aidd_project_memory> block in each
6:  * context file with two tiers:
7:  *   - Root memory files       -> always loaded, via a tool-appropriate reference.
8:  *   - internal/ and external/ -> listed (plain paths, no @), read on demand.
9:  *
10:  * Reference syntax for the always-loaded tier:
11:  *   CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md        -> @aidd_docs/memory/file.md
12:  *   .github/copilot-instructions -> [aidd_docs/memory/file.md](../aidd_docs/memory/file.md)
13:  *
14:  * Usage:
15:  *   node update_memory.js                  every context file already present
16:  *   node update_memory.js claude codex     only those tools' context files
17:  *
18:  * The auto hook calls it with no argument. The project-memory skill passes the
19:  * tools the user picked, so a context file the user did not choose is left
20:  * alone even when it exists.
21:  *
22:  * It only ever fills a block that is already there. Creating the file, or the
23:  * block inside it, is the skill's job.
24:  */
